osperous and the people living in it  more prosperous let me explain that what  that means how how do you do that i mean  like  better growth is sounds great doesn't it  i think everyone would agree with that  but but how do you do well you need you  need a number of things uh first of all  we've got to you were talking to nadeem  zahari about skill levels for example  we've still got 200 000 children  living in areas where there are no good  or outstanding schools the government's  actually having a debate with themselves  about sending not enough people i guess  too many people to university at the  same time  the question was how would labour tackle  inflation the windfall tax obviously is  something that we've talked about uh  every interview i talk about labour  front benches it's windfall tax but then  leaping towards schools as a way of  tackling inflation so it's not about  inflation it's a contributor to  long-term growth the skills of your  people also for example the green  transition that we've got to make  that can be a contributor to  long-term economic growth if we get it  right we match the technology the  capacity to make things here you need a  short-term plan at the moment to help  people with a cost of living crisis and  you need a long-term plan geared at the  country's prosperity um i guess i'm um  you know trying to work out a bit more  about the policy platform that labour  has i understand the windfall tax and  it's something that clearly you know you  can see government thinking about as  well um but it does feel like every time  i talk to labour all you talk about is  the windfall tax and the crisis is is  real as you say you know inflation at a  40-year high you want an emergency  budget you need something else in it  other than  let me give you another example if you  take costs for business which are a real  part of this right now we've advocated  more help for business rate relief paid  for by increasing the digital services  tax for t